{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On a large piece of paper, Dana creates a “rectangular spiral” by drawing line segments of lengths, in cm, of 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, ... as shown. Dana’s pen runs out of ink after the total of all the lengths he has drawn is 3000 cm. What is the length of the longest line segment that Dana draws?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031312eb2a8666378710aacc1b2d30bf00c06988.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 38 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 39 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 54 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 55 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\  50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are finding the sum of the integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> twice, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/2649ab2bdbd7224bde04463d84fb94048adfbf7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\frac{(n)(n+1)}{2} =  (n)(n+1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"216\" height=\"38\" /> We need to solve the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be26c3293946e93f017a2fa93d42fdb6f4e11a2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1) \\le 3000,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> which results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/703937fbea2a23e46d667e28db99ee890117619e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 54.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c30566eb8cdc9bedece6cf3fe5e9f72d50b979e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(C)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td><